  "1868 Hole-in-the-Day",
  "1870 The Crossing",
  "1936 Paul Bunyan parade",
  "1950 Talking Paul",
  "2003 The farm move",
  "1968 Donnybrooke",
  "1982 NHRA Nationals",
  "1986 Guy Doud",
  "1991 Ice Extravaganza",
];

const people = [
  { name: "Bagone-giizhig the Elder", role: "Mississippi Ojibwe", text: "Born about 1800 on Madeline Island. In 1836 he moved his band to Gull Lake and built a regional leadership the Americans treated as head chief. He died in 1847 when a wagon wheel crushed him at the Mississippi crossing at Little Falls.", photo: img.holeDag },
  { name: "Bagone-giizhig the Younger", role: "Hole-in-the-Day", text: "Born Gwiiwizens — Boy — about 1825. Took his father's name at twenty. Negotiated treaties, kept a house on Gull, and was shot on the road toward Crow Wing on June 27, 1868. The bay still carries the English name.", photo: img.hole },
  { name: "Guy Doud", role: "1986 National Teacher of the Year", text: "Wadena-born, Brainerd-raised. English at Brainerd High from 1975. On April 14, 1986, Reagan handed him the crystal apple at the White House. He said he taught because teachers had loved a kid the rest of the room had given up on. Later a speaker, pastor, and author of Molder of Dreams." },
  { name: "Sherm Levis", role: "Brought Paul north", text: "With Roy Kuemicheal he bought the Chicago Railroad Fair giant after the 1948–49 seasons and sat him at Highways 210 and 371. Oscar Larson hauled him up in pieces and bolted him together for the 1950 opening." },
