  { name: "Al Rademacher & Lois Moon", role: "Saved the giant", text: "Went to McFarland in 2003 to buy a train and a building for Dad's village. Walked out owning Paul, Babe, and the rides. Moved the 26-foot man on his back by trailer that September." },
  { name: "Jack & Jim Madden", role: "Gull Lake resort men", text: "Jack summered at Pine Beach in 1931, then leased a failing Depression golf course with uncle Tom for $500. The brothers bought it with nothing down and spent the next forty years turning a peninsula into Madden's." },
  { name: "Merrill & Louise Cragun", role: "Paul Bunyan Inc.", text: "In 1934 they registered Paul Bunyan Inc. to sell the lakes. With Jack Madden they staged the first Paul Bunyan parade in 1936. In 1940 they bought a swampy seven-acre hill on Steamboat Bay." },
  { name: "Dutch & Irma Cragun", role: "A legend on the lake", text: "Dutch's first job, at nine, was worms and minnows. He took over in 1957, married Irma in 1965, and built year-round rooms and 54 holes of golf. In 2025, at 93, he sold after 85 family years." },
  { name: "George Montgomery", role: "Donnybrooke builder", text: "A retired Northwest Airlines pilot who wanted somewhere to race his Shelby 427 Cobra. He carved a 3.1-mile course south of North Long Lake in 1968." },
  { name: "Jerry Hansen", role: "BIR's second life", text: "Winningest amateur in SCCA history. Bought the foreclosed track in 1973, renamed it Brainerd International Raceway, and put Mario Andretti on the board." },
